==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
Laugh (111).png|Dehydration/Heat Exposure
Krakken (2003).png|Electricity Vulnerability
</gallery>
{{Quote|Can't...breathe...need...water...|Ripjaws dehydrating.<ref name="SC" />}}
Ripjaws' greatest weakness is that he cannot stay on land for too long. If Ripjaws wants to stay on land, he would require water or cool temperatures<ref name="CF">''[[Clyde 5]]''</ref> to keep him from dehydrating. If he doesn't have any way of keeping himself hydrated for long enough, he could die. Exposure to extreme heat will cause Ripjaws to dehydrate even quicker.<ref name="LL" /><ref name="CF" />

Ripjaws is vulnerable to electricity.<ref name="TK" />

===Non-Canon Weaknesses===
====Cartoon Network Action Pack!====
Ripjaws is weak to mental attacks from beings that possess aquatic telepathy.{{Refn|''[[Aqua Nut]]''|group = AP}}

==History==
===Ben 10===
*Ripjaws first appeared in ''[[The Krakken]]'', where he helped the [[Krakken]] defeat [[Jonah Melville]] and retrieve her eggs.
*In ''[[Last Laugh]]'', Ripjaws defeated some crooks.
*In ''[[Secrets]]'', Ripjaws suffered from dehydration on [[Mt. Rushmore (Classic)|Mt. Rushmore]] and was nearly caught by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] before the malfunctioning [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] turned him into [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]].
**Also, Ripjaws appeared as one of the many alien templates used for Vilgax's army in an imaginary sequence.
*In ''[[Truth]]'', Ripjaws defeated a [[Havoc Beast]] and met [[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil]].
*In ''[[The Big Tick]]'', Ripjaws failed to defeat the [[Great One]].
*In ''[[Framed]]'', [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] mentioned Ripjaws was used by [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] to terrorize Chicago, Illinois.
*In ''[[They Lurk Below]]'', Ripjaws battled some [[Tentacle Trooper]]s.
*In ''[[Back With a Vengeance]]'', Ripjaws saved a drowning man before switching into [[Stinkfly (Classic)|Stinkfly]] to fly him to safety.
*In ''[[Divided We Stand]]'', Ripjaws went surfing and ended up scaring some tourists away from the beach.
*In ''[[Ben 4 Good Buddy]]'', Ripjaws fought the [[Road Crew]] and broke into [[Lawrence Wainright]]'s RV to find water.
*In ''[[Sleepaway Camper]]'', Ripjaws slept at the bottom of a lake to avoid [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]]'s snoring.

===Alien Force=== 
*Ripjaws was locked by the Omnitrix's reconfiguration in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]''.

===Ultimate Alien=== 
*In ''[[Deep]]'', Ripjaws was unlocked off-screen when the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] scanned some [[Piscciss Volann (Classic)|Piscciss Volann]].{{Refn|[[:File:Ben Scanned Piscciss Volanns.PNG]]|group = DM}}
*In ''[[Perplexahedron (Episode)|Perplexahedron]]'', Ripjaws broke himself and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] out of a room filled with water.
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Ripjaws appeared as one of the many aliens when Ben was explaining his story to [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]].

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Gone Fishin']]'', Ripjaws did some unsuccessful fishing. Later, Ripjaws went swimming with [[Patelliday]] and battled two [[Mechaneer]]s.
*In ''[[The Ballad of Mr. Baumann]]'', Ripjaws defeated [[Vulkanus]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Ripjaws appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

===Gwen 10 (What-If?)===
*In ''[[Gwen 10 (Episode)|Gwen 10]]'', [[Gwen Tennyson (Gwen 10)|Gwen]] used Ripjaws off-screen to catch some fish.

